+  <h3>Keyless static cipher used for all &ldquo;encrypted&rdquo; local secrets</h3>
+  <div class="grid2">
+    <div><h4>How it works</h4><p><code>com.bumptech.glide.d.p()</code> / <code>.q()</code> apply a fixed four-stage transform with no key material whatsoever: XOR every byte with <code>0x6C</code>; rotate each byte left by 3; reverse the whole buffer; XOR byte <em>i</em> with <code>(i*37) ^ 0xA5</code>. It was re-implemented in Python and round-trips perfectly. This single routine protects the Instagram password, the bearer token, the 2FA seed and every sensitive SharedPreferences value.</p></div>
