+<article class="vuln card" id="STOR-02" data-sev="Critical" data-cat="Data storage" data-search="stor-02 allowbackup=true with completely empty backup-exclusion rules data storage the manifest declares android:allowbackup=&quot;true&quot; with android:fullbackupcontent=&quot;@7f160000&quot; and android:dataextractionrules=&quot;@7f160001&quot; . both resources were decoded from the arsc and are empty shells: &lt;full-backup-content/&gt; (132 bytes) and &lt;data-extraction-rules&gt;&lt;cloud-backup/&gt;&lt;/data-extraction-rules&gt; (212 bytes). neither contains a single &lt;exclude&gt; element, so the default include-everything behaviour applies to the database and shared_prefs directories. the unencrypted room database instagram passwords, totp seeds, session tokens plus all of topfvc_shared , is copied into the user's google cloud backup and into any device-to-device transfer. an attacker who compromises the google account, or who borrows the phone during a migration, obtains every credential without ever touching the device. res/qq.xml = &lt;full-backup-content/&gt; ; res/4j.xml = &lt;data-extraction-rules&gt;&lt;cloud-backup/&gt;&lt;/data-extraction-rules&gt; ; out/21_backup_rules.txt set allowbackup=&quot;false&quot; , or add explicit &lt;exclude domain=&quot;database&quot; path=&quot;t_f_d_b_f_v_c&quot;/&gt; and &lt;exclude domain=&quot;sharedpref&quot; path=&quot;topfvc_shared.xml&quot;/&gt; to both rule files.">
