+<article class="vuln card" id="INTE-14" data-sev="Medium" data-cat="Integrity" data-search="inte-14 native anti-analysis relies on file reads and string matching; no ptrace, tracerpid, property_get, dlopen or timing checks exist integrity the claimed detection set does not match the binary. across all three abis the string tables contain no ptrace , no tracerpid , no /proc/self/status , no property_get or __system_property_get , no dlopen / dlsym , no prctl , no clock_gettime or gettimeofday . the 90-symbol import list confirms it: the only timing-adjacent import is clock , and the only syscall-adjacent ones are syscall , __open_2 , read , __read_chk , close and access . what the library actually does is read /proc/self/maps and match keywords that are stored xor-obfuscated with key 0x5a (recovered in work/out/19_xor_decoded.txt ), match base64-encoded frida markers decoding the .rodata base64 blobs yields libfrida-gadget , re.frida.server , gum-js-loop , substrate , libcso_substrate , libbridge.so , libc.so (deleted) and libart.so (deleted) and access() nine hardcoded su paths. there is no inline-hook detection, no svc-based syscall path, no debugger-attached check and no execution-timing check. every detection in the native layer is a filesystem read followed by a substring match, which is the weakest possible construction: it is defeated by sanitising the buffer returned from read() , by hooking strstr / strcmp , or by simply not having the target strings present. because there is no ptrace self-attach, no tracerpid parse and no timing check, a tracer can attach and single-step without ever tripping a detection. the obfuscation budget went entirely into control-flow flattening of code that performs trivially bypassable checks, so the anti-analysis story is far weaker than the binary's apparent sophistication suggests. string and import sweeps over all three abis; dt_needed = libz, libandroid, liblog, libm, libdl, libc; 90 imported symbols enumerated in work/out/30_aes_forensics_arm64.txt section 8; base64-decoded anti-analysis markers; xor key 0x5a keyword table in work/out/19_xor_decoded.txt treat detection as telemetry for server-side risk scoring rather than as a gate. if native detection is retained, add checks that cannot be satisfied by sanitising a file read hardware attestation verified server-side is the only construction that holds.">
