+    <div><h4>How it works</h4><p><code>ia.s.success()</code> decides the login outcome by string-searching the raw response body for <code>"Bearer"</code>, <code>"two_step_verification"</code>, <code>"challenge_required"</code>, <code>"The password you entered is incorrect"</code>, <code>"We can't find an account with"</code> and <code>"there was a problem with your request"</code>, and extracts the 2FA context with <code>indexOf("(dkc")</code> plus the regex <code>(\d+)\s+"com\.bloks\.</code>. <code>ia.v.a()</code> likewise splits on <code>"logged_in_user"</code>, <code>"headers"</code>, <code>"Bearer"</code> and <code>"hmac"</code>.</p></div>
