+    <div><h4>How it works</h4><p>The manifest sets <code>android:usesCleartextTraffic="false"</code> but declares no <code>android:networkSecurityConfig</code>. There is therefore no certificate-transparency requirement, no explicit trust-anchor restriction and no per-domain policy; on API 24+ user-installed CAs are excluded by default, but the app's own WebView and any debug-build behaviour is unconstrained.</p></div>
+    <div><h4>Impact</h4><p>The only transport control is the runtime-installed OkHttp pinner, which is itself hookable (TRAN-01) and remotely replaceable (TRAN-02). A declarative policy would at least survive Java-layer hooking.</p></div>
