++<article class="vuln card" id="CRED-02" data-sev="Critical" data-cat="Credentials" data-search="cred-02 2fa seed / backup codes stored in the two_factors table credentials a second room table two_factors holds u_n (username), u_p (password) and s_k (shared secret). c2.t issues the raw query select * from two_factors and populates twofactoraccount.setu_p() . s_k is the totp seed used by account/getsecretkey.php / requestdigitcode.php , and ha.c sends an s_k_2fa field to the backend. defeats two-factor authentication entirely: with the seed an attacker generates valid 6-digit codes forever. password (cred-01) plus this seed is a complete, permanent compromise. c2.t:627 s(&quot;select * from two_factors&quot;) , :660 setu_p(...) ; models.twofactoraccount.gets_k()/getu_p() ; addproperty(&quot;s_k_2fa&quot;, ...) never store a totp seed. if 2fa recovery is genuinely required, wrap it in an androidkeystore aes-gcm key bound to user authentication with hardware attestation.">
