++<article class="vuln card" id="CRED-03" data-sev="Critical" data-cat="Credentials" data-search="cred-03 webview cookie harvester synthesises an oauth bearer token from sessionid credentials oa.l1.onpagefinished() reads cookiemanager.getcookie(&quot;https://www.instagram.com/&quot;) , extracts sessionid , ds_user_id and mid , then builds &quot;bearer igt:2:&quot; + base64({&quot;ds_user_id&quot;:..,&quot;sessionid&quot;:..}) and writes it to instagram_accounts.u_a . this is silent session-token theft performed on any page load, with no user gesture or confirmation. account takeover without ever learning the password. the synthesised bearer is exactly what instagram's own mobile clients use, so it is fully functional for follow / like / comment / dm automation. oa.l1.java y(cookie,&quot;sessionid&quot;) , y(cookie,&quot;ds_user_id&quot;) , &quot;bearer igt:2:&quot; + base64.encodetostring(...) , v13_3.setu_a(com.bumptech.glide.d.q(v8_9)) do not harvest cookies from a webview. use official instagram oauth with pkce and store only the returned, scoped, expiring access token.">
