++<article class="vuln card" id="CRED-11" data-sev="Medium" data-cat="Credentials" data-search="cred-11 dead jni bridge: native code looks up helper.t.digest([b)[b which does not exist in the dex credentials at arm64 vas 0x106660 and 0x162c4c (and the equivalents at 0x106714 and 0x162ce0 ) libtopfollow.so executes ldr x8,[x8,#0x108] jnienv function-table slot 33, getstaticmethodid with x1 = the class ref for com/nivaroid/topfollow/helper/t , x2 = &quot;digest&quot; ( .rodata+0x14b88 ) and x3 = &quot;([b)[b&quot; ( .rodata+0x14cc4 ). enumerating the dex directly shows helper.t declares exactly two methods, o(ljava/lang/string;)ljava/lang/string; and sd(ljava/lang/string;)ljava/lang/string; . there is no digest method, and no method with descriptor ([b)[b exists in any com.nivaroid.topfollow class. the lookup therefore returns null and raises nosuchmethoderror . the native layer expects a java static byte[] digest(byte[]) that the shipped dex does not provide. that is a build-integrity defect: native and java halves of the app are out of step, so either a code path silently fails at runtime (and whatever protection or transform it was meant to perform does not happen), or the java class was stripped by an obfuscator that renamed or removed a method the native side still references by string. either way it demonstrates that the native/java contract is not verified at build time, and it is exactly the kind of mismatch an attacker can exploit by supplying their own digest implementation in a repackaged build to control what the native code believes it hashed. disassembly at 0x106644-0x106664 and 0x162c30-0x162c50 : ldr x8,[x8,#0x108] then add x2,x2,#0xb88 ( digest ), add x3,x3,#0xcc4 ( ([b)[b ), blr x8 ; dex enumeration of lcom/nivaroid/topfollow/helper/t; returning only o and sd ; zero ([b)[b methods in the app's packages add a build-time check that every findclass / get*methodid target in the native code exists in the compiled dex, and fail the build otherwise. exclude natively-referenced classes from obfuscator renaming.">
