+                                                    "OAEP"/"RSA" string; 0xE1000 is
+                                                    ordinary .rodata, RSA lives only
+                                                    in Java q8.t1 (PKCS#1 v1.5)
+ AES-GCM (native)                          ABSENT    no GHASH/H-table; GCM is Java-only
+ "18 MB" file                              FALSE     the file is 1,805,400 B = 1.72 MiB
+
+ What IS genuinely in the native library: the real AES forward S-box (0x128b0),
+ inverse S-box (0x139b0), rcon (0x13b10), a 549-byte key-derivation/whitening
+ table (0x13b30), and an AES-256-shaped key expansion (0x32158, rcon read 14x).
+ See report section 11 and findings CRYP-09 / CRYP-10.
+
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ THE REAL TRIPLE-LAYER STORY (vs the claimed one)
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ There is no Layer1(native PBKDF2) -> Layer2(native white-box AES-GCM) ->
+ Layer3(native RSA-OAEP) stack. The actual protection is:
+
+  * Local storage cipher (com.bumptech.glide.d.p()/q()): XOR 0x6C -> rotate-left
+    3 -> reverse -> XOR (i*37)^0xA5. KEYLESS. Round-trips in Python
+    (report/cipher_poc.py). This "encrypts" the on-device Instagram password and
+    2FA seed. (CRYP-01..04.)
